"url":"https://maurycyz.com/misc/email/","score":55,"flags":0,"comment_count":12,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"robalex","user_is_author":false,"tags":["email"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jnz4v5","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jnz4v5/bit_about_email"},{"short_id":"umsitb","created_at":"2026-11-08T11:07:51.827-06:00","title":"What can I realistically do with local AI on a Mac mini M5 Pro (48GB)?","url":"","score":23,"flags":9,"comment_count":11,"description":"\u003cp\u003eI just got a Mac mini with an M5 Pro (base CPU config) and 48GB of unified memory. I want to run as much AI locally as makes sense, but it's hard to separate what actually works day to day from benchmark hype.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I'd like to do:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCoding: autocomplete and agentic workflows with local models\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eImage generation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAnything else genuinely useful: transcription, RAG over my notes, etc.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eQuestions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhich models and quantizations fit comfortably in 48GB and are actually usable, not just \"it runs\"?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhich runtime and tools: MLX, llama.cpp, Ollama, LM Studio, ComfyUI, something else?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhat's your setup, and what did you give up on and go back to cloud APIs for?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReal tokens/sec numbers and \"this was a waste of time\" stories are especially welcome.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"I just got a Mac mini with an M5 Pro (base CPU config) and 48GB of unified memory. I want to run as much AI locally as makes sense, but it's hard to separate what actually works day to day from benchmark hype.\r\n\r\nWhat I'd like to do:\r\n\r\n- Coding: autocomplete and agentic workflows with local models\r\n- Image generation\r\n- Anything else genuinely useful: transcription, RAG over my notes, etc.\r\n\r\nQuestions:\r\n\r\n1. Which models and quantizations fit comfortably in 48GB and are actually usable, not just \"it runs\"?\r\n2. Which runtime and tools: MLX, llama.cpp, Ollama, LM Studio, ComfyUI, something else?\r\n3. What's your setup, and what did you give up on and go back to cloud APIs for?\r\n\r\nReal tokens/sec numbers and \"this was a waste of time\" stories are especially welcome.","submitter_user":"napolux","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","mac"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/umsitb","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/umsitb/what_can_i_realistically_do_with_local_ai"},{"short_id":"drozos","created_at":"2026-11-09T16:29:01.495-06:00","title":"Docker has always used microVMs (well, since 2016)","url":"https://dave.recoil.org/docker-has-always-used-microvms/","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"typesanitizer","user_is_author":false,"tags":["linux","osdev"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/drozos","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/drozos/docker_has_always_used_microvms_well"},{"short_id":"jqvofw","created_at":"2026-11-09T16:25:03.500-06:00","title":"Reverse engineering a vintage diode-transistor logic chip","url":"http://www.righto.com/2026/11/signetics-st680a-dtl-nand.html","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"calvin","user_is_author":false,"tags":["hardware","historical","reversing"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jqvofw","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/jqvofw/reverse_engineering_vintage_diode"}]